# =============================================================================
# .gitattributes — Line Ending Policy for CTF_Public
# =============================================================================
# ABOUT:
#   This file tells git how to handle line endings for every file in the repo.
#   It prevents Windows CRLF line endings from entering the repo regardless of
#   what platform a contributor is editing from.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS:
#   Shell scripts with CRLF line endings fail on Linux/macOS. The \r character
#   is invisible in most editors but the shell sees it — it becomes part of
#   variable values and heredoc terminators, causing silent misbehaviour.
#   A .gitattributes file is the single most reliable way to enforce LF across
#   all contributors without requiring them to configure git manually.
#
# HOW IT WORKS:
#   `text=auto` — git normalises line endings for all text files automatically.
#                 Files are stored as LF in the repo regardless of the platform.
#   `eol=lf`    — on checkout, git writes the file with LF endings even on
#                 Windows, rather than converting to CRLF.
#
# RESULT:
#   - Files in the repo always have LF endings (stored correctly)
#   - Files on disk after checkout always have LF endings (executed correctly)
#   - No manual `dos2unix` needed after cloning or pulling
#
# APPLYING TO AN EXISTING REPO:
#   After adding this file, run:
#     git add .gitattributes
#     git rm --cached -r .
#     git reset --hard
#   This re-normalises all tracked files using the new rules.
# =============================================================================

# --- Default: normalise all text files to LF ----------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Shell scripts: explicitly enforce LF -------------------------------------
# These are the files most at risk from CRLF causing runtime failures.
*.sh text eol=lf

# --- Markdown and config files: enforce LF ------------------------------------
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.env  text eol=lf

# --- Binary files: no line ending conversion ----------------------------------
# Tell git these are binary so it never attempts conversion.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.tar  binary
*.gz   binary